# Research loop

Core loop: OBSERVE → HYPOTHESIZE → DESIGN → TRAIN → EVALUATE → REMEMBER → SELECT → REPEAT

The bounded research engine must: inspect prior results, propose configs, build networks, train, measure, compare to independent references, reject failures, keep validated gains, and use evidence for the next experiment.

Self-improvement is a **measured** claim. Autonomy stays inside fixed resource limits, validated design schemas, and independent evaluation rules. The agent must not change its own permissions, safety constraints, evaluation rules, or financial risk limits.

## Continual learning

Investigate transfer, meta-learning, few-shot adaptation, replay, EWC, catastrophic-forgetting mitigation, hierarchical RL, world models, causal representations, modular intelligence, and learning-to-learn. Do not optimize only one demo env. Evaluate on multiple independent tasks. Ask whether skills transfer across domains.

## Measurement

Compare every change to baselines. Explain how improvements will be measured. Prefer computationally cheap local experiments. Complexity without measurable gain is not success. Prevent leakage, benchmark gaming, and self-evaluation without an independent check.
